## Context

Author imagine (2026-06-06, during the 0446 figure review): "an active
version to spot check the matcher. When I hover on a cell, it popups the
reference list vs model reply comparison table (name, fuel, capacity,
status, level)."

Use case is matcher QA, not publication: a recognized cell shows *what* the
LP matcher paired (reference row vs the model's emitted row, with the match
costs); a miss shows the nearest rejected candidates; an FP cell shows why
the emission was vetoed. This turns FP investigation (cf. 0445 mở-rộng
extension suffix, name-variant failures behind the "unrecognized" framing)
from grepping JSON into pointing at the picture.

## Pistes

- Artifact: standalone HTML (plotly heatmap with customdata hover, or
  hand-rolled SVG+JS) generated by a sibling of `plot_exp1_matrix` from the
  same `exp1_recognition` derivation — same data, second renderer; never a
  replacement for the committed PDF.
- Per-cell payload: reference row (name, fuel, capacity, status, level) vs
  matched model row, LP similarity and capacity-delta costs, match type.
  `level` is the 0401/0402 column (post-preprint) — degrade gracefully while
  it does not exist.
- The derivation must expose the matched pair, not just the boolean —
  `RecognitionCell` currently keeps `recognized` only; extend with the
  matched system row (or a match-detail sidecar) without breaking the
  figure/table consumers.
- Makefile: data-dependent single output (one HTML), normal DAG rule; the
  artifact is a dev tool — decide whether it is committed or gitignored
  (handoff-artifact rule says commit only if something downstream consumes
  it).

## Exit criteria (to sharpen at Plan)

- [ ] Hovering any cell shows the reference-vs-reply comparison table
- [ ] FP cells show the veto/rejection detail
- [ ] Generated via the DAG from records + reference, no side-outputs
- [ ] Author spot-check session: at least one matcher verdict overturned or
      confirmed using only the interactive view

## Related

- 0446 (static matrix), 0445 (extension-suffix FP investigation)
- 0401/0402 (level column)
